            <ArticleTitle>Ruthenium(II)-Catalyzed Redox-Neutral Oxidative Cyclization of Benzimidates with Alkenes with Hydrogen Evolution.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6678-6681</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03405</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>1H-Isoindoles and 2H-isoindoles are synthesized via a ruthenium-catalyzed oxidant-free cyclization of benzimidates with alkenes at room temperature with the liberation of H2. Later, 1H-isoindoles were converted into nitrogen-containing heterocycles. The proposed reaction mechanism was strongly supported by experimental evidence and DFT calculations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
